                <pb facs="0592" n="582" xml:id="pg582"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.50 Recovery/6–2748: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Stuart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Nanking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1948-06-27T13:00:00+09:00">June 27, 1948—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 27—8:43 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1165. In conference this morning with Foreign Office, Embassy’s revised text
                    article IV (old numbering) rejected. RefEmbtel 1163 and 1164, June 27, 11 a.m.
                    Embassy requests authority <hi rendition="#italic">in extremis</hi> to revert to
                    original language this article and secure strict and detailed interpretative
                    commitment in agreed minute of negotiators.</p>
                <p>Sent Dept 1165; repeated Shanghai 536.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stuart</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
